# Recorded and derived data. books.jsonl is ~45 GB per slate and the viewer
# tree is ~65 GB across ~64,000 files -- far past GitHub's limits, and all of
# it is reproducible from the recorder output. Only the small MLB Stats API
# window file and the analysis results are worth committing (see the
# project-level .gitignore for those exceptions).
polymarket_orderbook/data/live/
polymarket_orderbook/data/viewer_full/
polymarket_orderbook/data/uniform/
polymarket_orderbook/data/plots/
polymarket_orderbook/data/discovery_cache.json

# The recorder also writes to the ROOT data/live/, which this file listed only
# under polymarket_orderbook/. That gap left 133 GB across four books_*.jsonl
# visible to `git add -A`:
#   data/live/books_2026-08-28.jsonl          43.63 GB
#   data/live/books_2026-08-29.jsonl          43.01 GB
#   data/live/books_2026-08-30.jsonl          25.41 GB
#   data/live/books_2026-08-27.jsonl.jsonl    21.13 GB
# Every one is far past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, so a push would have
# failed after uploading gigabytes. Caught with:
#   git status --porcelain -uall
# which expands untracked directories -- plain `git status` collapses them to
# a single line and hides the size entirely.
data/live/

# Generated viewer page: rebuilt by build_viewer_multi.py, churns every run.
polymarket_orderbook/viewer_full.html

# mlbmodel: API response cache and derived tables. Everything here is
# reproducible from the free APIs with `python -m mlbmodel.collect` and
# `python -m mlbmodel.odds`; only reports/ is worth committing.
data/raw/
data/processed/
reports/predictions.parquet
reports/slate_*.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Logs
*.log
polymarket_orderbook/logs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-09-16: a second round of oversized artefacts. `git status --porcelain
# -uall` showed 14.17 GB across 391 untracked files, several individually past
# GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit. All of it is either downloaded or
# regenerable, so none of it belongs in the repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Kaggle downloads and their extraction scratch space (4.3 GB + 2.9 GB + 780 MB
# of zips, plus duplicated parquet trees under the pipeline run dirs).
kaggle_sports_download/
kaggle_cross_market_download/
kaggle_sports_pipeline/
kaggle_metadata_full/
cross_market_universe/

# The polymarket_sports tick dataset: ~4.0 GB of orderbook parquet and 0.32 GB
# of snapshots. Reproducible from the Kaggle source. The small metadata table
# and the reports ARE kept (see the negations below).
polymarket_sports/orderbook/
polymarket_sports/snapshots/
polymarket_sports/trades/

# Generated research caches: minute panels, sequence tensors, move tables.
# Rebuilt by the build_* scripts in each research folder.
polymarket_orderbook/research/*/cache/

# Per-row jump tables. lee_mykland_jumps.csv is 175-176 MB per variant, past
# the per-file limit; the summaries and metric tables next to it are kept.
polymarket_orderbook/results/lee_mykland/**/lee_mykland_jumps.csv
polymarket_orderbook/results/makinen/jumps/lee_mykland_jumps.csv
polymarket_orderbook/results/makinen/**/replay_events.csv
polymarket_orderbook/results/makinen/preds/*.npy
polymarket_orderbook/results/makinen/preds/*.pt
polymarket_orderbook/results/makinen/**/preds_*.npy
polymarket_orderbook/results/jump_prediction/*.npy
polymarket_orderbook/results/jump_prediction/allbooks_run_*/
